11
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,500
You're going to give a short speech of thanks for the speaker this evening, aren't

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,140
you, Bill? Yes.

13
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,660
You don't sound very enthusiastic.

14
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,740
It's not that bad, it?

15
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:01,200
No, I don't mind really, but I can never forget the first speech of thanks I did.

16
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:02,600
Why? What happened?

17
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,240
Well, I was in my early 20s.

18
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,580
I joined the Local History Society.

19
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:11,840
Yes. Anyway, I went along to a lecture by a Miss Bly.

20
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,500
Oh, do go on.

21
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,980
She was going to talk, with slides, about our town in the 18th century.

22
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:22,720
She'd just published a book on the subject, which was reckoned to be quite good.

23
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:24,700
So, I went along.

24
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:29,660
When I arrived, the secretary asked me if I could give the speech of thanks.

25
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,660
Rather stupidly, I said yes.

26
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:34,640
We've all done it.

27
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,740
Anyway, from that point on, I was scared.

28
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,340
What should I say?

29
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:45,160
I decided to make notes during the lecture and refer to interesting parts and thank

30
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,480
her on behalf of the Society.

31
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:51,760
In fact, by the time Miss Bly stood up to talk, I was feeling much better.

32
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,880
But she was so nervous that she kept forgetting what to say.

33
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,540
And she spoke almost in a whisper.

34
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:02,440
People at the back kept calling out, can't hear.

35
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,060
It was embarrassing.

36
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,840
can imagine it.

37
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,720
At least the slides were good.

38
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:12,920
That is, until the bulb in the projector blew and she had to finish the talk with no

39
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,500
illustrations. So what did you say in your speech of thanks?

40
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,100
What can you say?

41
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,700
You have to be polite.

42
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:25,060
I mentioned the interesting facts, referred to the excellent slides, and then

43
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:30,320
finished up by saying, we'd all like to thank Miss Bly for blowing us her slides.

44
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,980
Oh, no. I felt terrible.

45
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:36,540
I tried to apologize, not very successfully.

46
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,900
And the speech of thanks this evening?

47
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:44,100
I'll write down exactly what I'm going to say and read it carefully.

48
