00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:43,020
When purchasing life insurance, there are many important factors to consider.

178
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:49,040
One should buy the policies that give the most protection at the least cost, ensure

179
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:53,140
the right family members, and consider the family's financial needs.

180
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:58,620
It is important to buy the insurance from companies that are financially sound and

181
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:01,740
that are represented by honest, well -trained agents.

182
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:13,240
At various stages in a person's life, different kinds of life insurance are Probably

183
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:18,800
the only life insurance he needs is enough to cover his debts and burial expenses.

184
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:25,220
can be purchased at a lower rate during the young years, but by buying while young,

185
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:28,320
the premiums are paid in for a longer period of time.

186
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:32,220
In the end, the amount paid for premiums is about the same.

187
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:36,360
A person shouldn't buy insurance protection that really isn't necessary.

188
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:41,600
Suppose that Jerry marries Jeanette, who is a college graduate and is working.

189
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:46,380
Perhaps enough insurance would be needed to cover their debts and burial expenses.

190
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:51,380
Now, Jeanette has quit work, and their first child is on way.

191
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:56,140
They have purchased a home with a small down payment and a 30 -year mortgage.

192
00:15:56,940 --> 00:16:00,120
The situation regarding life insurance takes on a different look.

193
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,160
There are dependents who need financial protection.

194
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,640
How much insurance is needed?

195
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:10,780
As the family increases in size, it is essential to add more insurance on the

196
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:12,060
breadwinner to protect the

197
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:17,560
dependents. When the children are young and depend upon the family for financial

198
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:22,460
needs, families with modest incomes have difficulty providing enough life insurance

199
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:24,380
to protect the mother and the children.

200
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:30,480
Families with modest incomes should ensure the breadwinner or breadwinners first.

201
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:35,780
When considering the amount of insurance for the mother with dependent children,

202
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:42,100
substitute child care is a need that should be planned for until the children can

203
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,240
care for themselves.

204
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:48,880
The death of a small child would have no effect upon the income of the family.

205
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:55,100
Perhaps a policy to meet funeral expenses would be sufficient for the young child,

206
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:58,940
although most people do not take out insurance on their young children.

207
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:03,340
As the children become financially independent of the family,

208
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:10,580
the emphasis on family financial security will shift from protection to saving for

209
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:11,900
the retirement years.

210
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:18,020
Every family situation is different, but it is important that each family give

211
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:20,980
adequate thought to planning its financial future.

